{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/266374-sell-me-on-hunter-2nd-edition","id":266374,"title":"Sell me on Hunter: 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-26T12:50:58-07:00","id":266374,"title":"Sell me on Hunter: 2nd Edition","content":"Don't get me wrong. I like the idea of it. I love playing monster-hunters, and mortals who stumble onto something bigger, and gutter occultists scrambling to understand what they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> I like being able to understand and even utilize <i>small </i>elements of the supernatural, without playing as a full-blown monster.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'm the guy rooting for Batman in even the most over-the-top super-villain fight.<br /> <br /> But ... I have the Mystery Cult and Exotic Armory merits, and the Ephemeral Entities rules, and Integrity. I already <i>have</i> my Endowments, and Tactics, and Codes, and Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> What would a putative Second Edition of Hunter have, that goes <i>beyond</i> GMC core?<br /> <br /> Discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T14:53:46-07:00","id":266440,"title":"","content":"The biggest sell to me would be redoing the Endowments systems completely. Divorce the Tier-as-scale from Tier-as-power-level thing so smaller groups with Endowments is easier to do. Get away from trying to squeeze Endowments into the Merits systems (esp. as you note the GMC has a lot of that taken care of anyway).<br /> <br /> Also the new WP gambling rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:02:42-07:00","id":266463,"title":"","content":"I make no lie that my favourite part of hunter are the organisations, and 2nd Edition would give a chance to knock of a few really rough edges. Without going into much detail or specific orgs.<br /> <br /> 1) The lack of any real support for actually playing a Tier 2 or Tier 3 story. There's no mechanics for operating at that scale, and far more importantly, there's virtually no fluff explaining how the organisations are... well organised. Adding a new section (or replacing the Hunters section if space is too limited) that gives an outline of each groups organisational structure and their general strategy would be a massive improvement.<br /> <br /> 2) Explicitly setting a theme and mood for each organisation. Sometimes &quot;alone and ignorant against the darkness&quot; suits TF:V, and sometimes they're flying a black helicopter loaded with inferno missiles towards a vampire prince. I get the feeling that there are occasions where TF:V has been forced square-peg-round-hole into &quot;alone and ignorant against the darkness&quot;, it would be better if there was a nice round hole for every organisation.<br /> <br /> 3) A clear separation between Hunters who have and who have not been subverted by monsters. My preferred version will be to present each organisation once with a full write up that portrays them as un-subverted. Then in the antagonists chapter have a paragraph detailing an alternative version of the organisation that is under a monster's sway.<br /> <br /> Note that I don't consider minor templates like Ghouls to be &quot;monsters&quot;. Morally dubious, sure, but still human. I'd also make a special exception for God being in control of the Long Night and the MM; provided that 1) A reasonable interpretation of the books could say that he's not actually in control. 2) A reasonable interpretation of the books could say that it's a good thing for humanity that he is in control. I am ok with additional interpretations on top of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing that Hunter could do that isn't in God Machine Core. Religion. I don't know if it's intentional, but here's a list of religious organisations in Hunter: Ahl al-Jabal, Long Night, Ascending Ones, The Faithful of Shulpae, Knights of Saint Adrian, Knights of Saint George, Les Mysteres, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum<br /> <br /> And here's a list of the explicitly Abrahamic religious groups: Ahl al-Jabal, Long Night, Ascending Ones, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum<br /> <br /> Out of twelve official Conspiracies, <b>seven! </b>are explicitly religious. That's the majority. Out of the corebook, three of six are explicitly Abrahamic! Obviously I'm counting the Ascending Ones as 1 rather than 1/3<br /> <br /> <br /> As I said, I don't know if it's intentional, but Hunter has a ton of religion in there. And currently, it's handled pretty badly. There are points where Malleus Maleficarum write up gets really basic parts of Catholicism wrong (Flyboy is the person to ask; though I can say the Mummy section in Mortal Remains is one example). There's practically nothing in Hunter for Abrahamic angels, there is actually nothing at all for non-Abrahamic Gods (sorry Ascending Ones). The Demon write up in Mortal Remains actually makes it harder to use Inferno for antagonists (yes I know you can ignore it; my point is to illustrate how little support Hunter gives for religious demons instead of G-M demons).<br /> <br /> <br /> At the very least hunter should support the following kinds of monsters: Abrahamic angels. Abrahamic demons. Egyptian Gods. In short, the monsters with explicit ties to a core 12 org. The best way to do it would probably be creating an equivilent to WoD Inferno (the concept of a template applied to different kids Ephemerial being will work as well for gods/angels as for demons), then putting in a little bit of support for tying WoD Inferno and WoD Empyrean into Hunter.<br /> <br /> Though I would also like to see hunter acknowledge that, intentionally or not, religion is now a theme and giving advice for it.<br /> <br /> ===============<br /> <br /> edit: I was ninjaed by Heavy Arms, but I agree with what he said. (Well I would, wouldn't I <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ref Hunter Cults)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-26-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:45:03-07:00","id":266488,"title":"","content":"&gt;As I said, I don't know if it's intentional, but Hunter has a ton of religion in there. And currently, it's handled pretty badly. There are points where Malleus Maleficarum write up gets really basic parts of Catholicism wrong (Flyboy is the person to ask; though I can say the Mummy section in Mortal Remains is one example). There's practically nothing in Hunter for Abrahamic angels, there is actually nothing at all for non-Abrahamic Gods (sorry Ascending Ones).<br /> <br /> I would say the lucifuge is more tied to occultism than abrahamic religions and, like it or not, the abrahamic religions have been the most influential ones in recent centuries. Of course, if they got parts of catholicism wrong in the MM right up that should definitely be corrected, I don't know enough about the religion to say.<br /> <br /> ......Though I don't know why you think hunter lacks support for abrahamic demons, hunter core has a full section devoted to them, I prefer it to inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T19:38:50-07:00","id":266568,"title":"","content":"It really doesn't bother me that MM or any other religiously intertwined Hunter org. gets the religious aspect part of it 100% of the time. I'm not expecting theologically written sourcebooks written by religious professors. Loosely based info that's enough for me to chew on and/or get the gist of a conspiracy/compact/cell is good enough for me.<br /> <br /> I agree with what Heavy Arms stated.<br /> <br /> For me? Just give me Hunter,with updated GMC rules(like the endowments), and I'm a happy camper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T04:52:11-07:00","id":266715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjasantaclause</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/266374-sell-me-on-hunter-2nd-edition?p=266488#post266488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the lucifuge is more tied to occultism than abrahamic religions</div> </div> </div> </div> It dosn't matter which one is &quot;more&quot;. They're still tied to Satan and thus Abrahamic myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjasantaclause</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/266374-sell-me-on-hunter-2nd-edition?p=266488#post266488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">......Though I don't know why you think hunter lacks support for abrahamic demons, hunter core has a full section devoted to them, I prefer it to inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a mixture of Inferno and Unchained - the writers have said themselves that Mr White is an Unchained. Though I will agree that hunter core supports Abrahamic demons a lot better than mortal remains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/266374-sell-me-on-hunter-2nd-edition?p=266568#post266568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really doesn't bother me that MM or any other religiously intertwined Hunter org. gets the religious aspect part of it 100% of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd be happy if they got the basics right. It's not like I could tell if they got anything more complicated wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T05:24:31-07:00","id":266722,"title":"","content":"King's Raven: you're saying that Hunter 2.0 could be filled with sample characters, monsters, and organisations rather than new mechanics?<br /> <br /> So, rather than giving us shiny new rules for &quot;demons&quot; and &quot;angels&quot; when we already have Ephemeral Entities, it would contain a a few lines of mechanics and a whole lot of Abrahamic fluff for them. (Hopefully several, speaking as someone with an abiding interest in the various Abrahamic demonologies.) Rather than giving us a rehash of the Mystery Cult rules, it would give us lots of useful ready-made details how the various Compacts and Conspiracies organize and conduct themselves.<br /> <br /> I guess I could get behind that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-27-2014, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T08:05:54-07:00","id":266762,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that's a great idea. We already have books and books of rules for monsters, most of which get republished in a highly simplified form in the Hunter books. If Hunter was actually designed on the assumption that you'd combine it with either: The actual monster books or a seperate book (call it Hunter: Beastry*) that would free up a <b>TON</b> of wordcount for stuff that's completely unique to hunter.<ul><li>More Endowments / more elaborate endowments.</li> <li>More details on the organisations - the stuff you need to portray them as an actual organisation.</li> <li>Filling in the gaps. There's no book that actually covers the Abrahamic God, so for MM/Long Night/Knife of Paradise players here's an option for makeing Him the guy your hunter worships, an option for making Him genuine but flawed, an imposter, and here's the possibilities for him being an established thing (Spirit, Supernal God, Exarch, etc). Same for the Lucifuge and Satan and the Southern Temple and the Egyptian Gods. Or for a non-religious example: Here's some breakthroughs a Null Mysteriis player might contribute towards. (I would definately say that when presetning a list of options for something core to a Compact/Conspiracy's self identity. One option has to be the Compact/Conspiracy are completely right)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Basically: Chapter 1: a big list of dread powers. Chapter 2: Advice for building monsters (how to build a charismatic manipulator, how to balance a combat encounter, etc). Chapter 3: A basic outline of every PC monster and the most important antagonists (think hunter Core's write up on Changelings or Slashers), plus advice for which Dread Powers they should have, plus really basic rules for important special mechanics like the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T09:45:29-07:00","id":266816,"title":"","content":"&gt;A clear separation between Hunters who have and who have not been subverted by monsters. My preferred version will be to present each organisation once with a full write up that portrays them as un-subverted. Then in the antagonists chapter have a paragraph detailing an alternative version of the organisation that is under a monster's sway.<br /> <br /> &gt;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Filling in the gaps. There's no book that actually covers the Abrahamic God, so for MM/Long Night/Knife of Paradise players here's an option for makeing Him the guy your hunter worships, an option for making Him genuine but flawed, an imposter, and here's the possibilities for him being an established thing (Spirit, Supernal God, Exarch, etc). Same for the Lucifuge and Satan and the Southern Temple and the Egyptian Gods. Or for a non-religious example: Here's some breakthroughs a Null Mysteriis player might contribute towards. (I would definately say that when presetning a list of options for something core to a Compact/Conspiracy's self identity. One option has to be the Compact/Conspiracy are completely right)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Hoo boy. I'm <i>quite </i>solidly sold now.<br /> <br /> Gosh, but a lot of cool ideas are springing to mind.<br /> <br /> Have you considered doing a fan book of this? A sort of &quot;how to God-Machine your Hunter game up, whut whut!&quot;? (Only ... more so, I guess.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T09:50:35-07:00","id":266820,"title":"","content":"I've considered doing a fangame of most things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm unlikely to do a Hunter 2.0, because it will be overshadowed by the official release, but if other people contributed then I would definitely join in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T11:35:15-07:00","id":267542,"title":"","content":"I agree with TKR, I would like them to add more stuff to religion, also how does <b>Empyrean Chronicles </b> sound to you guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T12:05:29-07:00","id":267557,"title":"","content":"A little <i>too</i> much religion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I want religion for the Long Night, Lucifuge, the MM and the Knife of Paradise (plus the non-core religious groups). I don't want religion to work it's way into, say, TF:V. I mean, if you want to take that VALKARIE literally then sure, but not by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}